    "title": "Insert a Value into a List at a Specific Index",
    "description": "Complete the ListEditor class by implementing the insertAndFormat(List<String> items, int index, String value) method.\n\nA List is an ordered collection, so inserting at a given integer index must keep the element order consistent. The method must:\n- insert value at the given index in the list\n- return the updated list as one string, with elements separated by a single space\n\nDuplicate values are allowed and must remain in the list.\n\nThe main method reads:\n- an integer n\n- n strings for the initial list\n- an integer index\n- one string value\n\nThen it prints the returned result.",
