    "title": "Count Increases While Traversing an Array with a Pointer",
    "description": "Write a C program that reads an integer n and then reads n integers into an array.\n\nTraverse the array using a pointer. Count how many elements are greater than the element immediately before them.\n\nFor example, in the array 3 5 2 7 7, the increasing positions are 5 > 3 and 7 > 2, so the result is 2.\n\nInput:\n- The first line contains an integer n (1 <= n <= 100).\n- The second line contains n integers.\n\nOutput:\n- Print the number of elements that are greater than the previous element.",
    "source_chunk_ids": ["6a7f572e5975329719be788a", "6a7f572e5975329719be7889"],
    "skeleton_code": [
      {
        "filename": "main.c",
        "content": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main(void) {\n    int n;\n    int a[100];\n    int i;\n\n    scanf(\"%d\", &n);\n    for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        scanf(\"%d\", &a[i]);\n    }\n\n    return 0;\n}\n",
        "is_readonly": false
      }
    ],
    "solution_code": [
      {
        "filename": "main.c",
        "content": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main(void) {\n    int n;\n    int a[100];\n    int i;\n    int count = 0;\n    int *p;\n    int *end;\n\n    scanf(\"%d\", &n);\n    for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        scanf(\"%d\", &a[i]);\n    }\n\n    if (n > 1) {\n        end = a + n;\n        for (p = a + 1; p < end; p++) {\n            if (*p > *(p - 1)) {\n                count++;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", count);\n    return 0;\n}\n"
      }
    ],
