    "type": "PE",
    "topic_tags": ["abstract classes", "polymorphism", "inheritance", "method overriding"],
    "difficulty": "Easy",
    "title": "Implement an Abstract Appliance Class with Overridden Status Behavior",
    "description": "Complete the program so that it uses an abstract class and overridden methods.\n\nRequirements:\n- Create an abstract class named Appliance with a boolean field named on.\n- The Appliance constructor receives the initial state.\n- Provide a method isOn() that returns the current state.\n- Declare an abstract method getStatus().\n- Class Fan extends Appliance and overrides getStatus():\n  - return \"Fan: spinning\" when the appliance is on\n  - return \"Fan: stopped\" when the appliance is off\n- Class AirConditioner extends Appliance and overrides getStatus():\n  - return \"AirConditioner: cooling\" when the appliance is on\n  - return \"AirConditioner: idle\" when the appliance is off\n\nThe main method reads two integers:\n- the first integer is 1 or 0 for the fan state\n- the second integer is 1 or 0 for the air conditioner state\n\nCreate the two objects using Appliance references and print their statuses on separate lines.",
    "source_chunk_ids": ["6a802c746b075af21f751835", "6a802c746b075af21f751833"],
    "skeleton_code": [
      {
        "filename": "Main.java",
        "content": "import java.util.*;\n\nabstract class Appliance {\n    private boolean on;\n\n    public Appliance(boolean on) {\n        this.on = on;\n    }\n\n    public boolean isOn() {\n        return false;\n    }\n\n    public abstract String getStatus();\n}\n\nclass Fan extends Appliance {\n    public Fan(boolean on) {\n        super(on);\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public String getStatus() {\n        return \"\";\n    }\n}\n\nclass AirConditioner extends Appliance {\n    public AirConditioner(boolean on) {\n        super(on);\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public String getStatus() {\n        return \"\";\n    }\n}\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int fanInput = sc.nextInt();\n        int acInput = sc.nextInt();\n\n        Appliance fan = new Fan(fanInput == 1);\n        Appliance airConditioner = new AirConditioner(acInput == 1);\n\n        System.out.println(fan.getStatus());\n        System.out.println(airConditioner.getStatus());\n    }\n}\n",
        "is_readonly": false
      }
    ],
    "solution_code": [
      {
        "filename": "Main.java",
        "content": "import java.util.*;\n\nabstract class Appliance {\n    private boolean on;\n\n    public Appliance(boolean on) {\n        this.on = on;\n    }\n\n    public boolean isOn() {\n        return on;\n    }\n\n    public abstract String getStatus();\n}\n\nclass Fan extends Appliance {\n    public Fan(boolean on) {\n        super(on);\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public String getStatus() {\n        if (isOn()) {\n            return \"Fan: spinning\";\n        }\n        return \"Fan: stopped\";\n    }\n}\n\nclass AirConditioner extends Appliance {\n    public AirConditioner(boolean on) {\n        super(on);\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public String getStatus() {\n        if (isOn()) {\n            return \"AirConditioner: cooling\";\n        }\n        return \"AirConditioner: idle\";\n    }\n}\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int fanInput = sc.nextInt();\n        int acInput = sc.nextInt();\n\n        Appliance fan = new Fan(fanInput == 1);\n        Appliance airConditioner = new AirConditioner(acInput == 1);\n\n        System.out.println(fan.getStatus());\n        System.out.println(airConditioner.getStatus());\n    }\n}\n"
      }
