    "description": "Write a Java program that simulates the probe path of quadratic probing in an open-address hash table.\n\nFor each query key x in a table of size M, compute h(x) = x % M and then visit positions in this order:\n(h(x) + 0^2) % M,\n(h(x) + 1^2) % M,\n(h(x) + 2^2) % M, ...\n\nStop when the next position has already been visited before. For each key, print the number of distinct table positions visited.\n\nInput:\n- The first line contains two integers M and q\n- The second line contains q non-negative integers\n\nOutput:\n- Print q integers separated by one space\n- Each integer is the number of distinct positions visited for the corresponding key\n\nNotes:\n- You only need to simulate the probe sequence, not insert elements into the table\n- Assume M > 0 and q >= 1",
