    "title": "Print the Unique Slots Visited by Quadratic Probing",
    "description": "Write a Java program that reads two integers M and x. Use the hash function h(x) = x % M, then generate the quadratic probing sequence\n\npos(i) = (h(x) + i * i) % M   for i = 0, 1, 2, ...\n\nPrint each visited slot in order, but stop before printing a slot that has already appeared earlier in the sequence. Output the visited slots on one line, separated by a single space.\n\nThis task shows that quadratic probing may revisit positions before covering every slot.\n\nInput:\n- Two integers M and x\n\nOutput:\n- The unique visited slots in probing order, separated by spaces",
    "source_chunk_ids": ["6a81d7efd103f7044396559f"],
    "skeleton_code": [
      {
        "filename": "Main.java",
        "content": "import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int M = sc.nextInt();\n        int x = sc.nextInt();\n\n        // Write your code here\n    }\n}\n",
        "is_readonly": false
      }
    ],
    "solution_code": [
      {
        "filename": "Main.java",
        "content": "import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int M = sc.nextInt();\n        int x = sc.nextInt();\n\n        int h = x % M;\n        Set<Integer> visited = new HashSet<>();\n        List<Integer> result = new ArrayList<>();\n\n        int i = 0;\n        while (true) {\n            int pos = (h + i * i) % M;\n            if (visited.contains(pos)) {\n                break;\n            }\n            visited.add(pos);\n            result.add(pos);\n            i++;\n        }\n\n        for (int j = 0; j < result.size(); j++) {\n            if (j > 0) System.out.print(\" \");\n            System.out.print(result.get(j));\n        }\n    }\n}\n"
      }
    ],
