    "title": "Check Reachability of a Slot in Quadratic Probing",
    "description": "In an open-address hash table, quadratic probing visits positions using the rule:\n\npos(i) = (h + i * i) % M   for i = 0, 1, 2, ...\n\nBecause quadratic probing may revisit old positions before covering the whole table, not every slot is always reachable.\n\nWrite a Java program that reads three integers M, h, and target.\n- M is the table size.\n- h is the starting hash position.\n- target is the slot you want to check.\n\nGenerate the probing sequence in order. Stop as soon as a position repeats.\n- If target appears in the sequence before any repetition, print FOUND followed by the first step index i where it appears.\n- Otherwise, print NOT_FOUND followed by the number of distinct positions visited before the repetition happens.\n\nInput:\n- Three integers: M h target\n\nOutput:\n- FOUND i\nor\n- NOT_FOUND k\nwhere k is the number of distinct visited positions.",
    "source_chunk_ids": ["6a81d7efd103f7044396559f"],
