    "description": "Write a Java program that manages a queue of integers using an array-based circular queue.\n\nThe queue starts with a given initial capacity m.\n\nCommands:\n- ADD x : insert x at the rear of the queue\n- TAKE : remove and print the front value; print -1 if the queue is empty\n- PEEK : print the front value without removing it; print -1 if the queue is empty\n\nQueue rules:\n- The queue is empty when first = -1.\n- The queue is full when (first == 0 && last == max - 1) or first == last + 1.\n- When adding to a full queue, grow the array to max + max / 2 and keep the logical order from front to rear.\n- For insertion, if last == max - 1 or last == -1, place the new value at index 0 and set last = 0. If the queue was empty, first also becomes 0. Otherwise insert at ++last.\n- For removal, if the queue has only one element, set first = last = -1 after removing it. Otherwise, if first == max - 1, move first to 0; else increase first by 1.\n\nInput:\n- The first line contains two integers m and q.\n- The next q lines each contain one command.\n\nOutput:\n- For every TAKE or PEEK command, print one line.\n- After processing all commands, print the remaining queue from front to rear on one line, separated by one space.\n- If the queue is empty at the end, print EMPTY.",
