    "description": "Write a Java program that manages a queue stored in an array of fixed size N using circular indexing.\n\nUse two integer variables:\n- first: index of the front element\n- last: index of the last element\n\nInitial state:\n- first = -1\n- last = -1\n\nA queue is empty when first == -1.\nA queue is full when either:\n- first == 0 and last == N - 1, or\n- first == last + 1\n\nInput:\n- The first line contains two integers N and Q: the queue capacity and the number of commands.\n- The next Q lines each contain one command:\n  - ENQUEUE x : insert integer x at the rear if the queue is not full\n  - DEQUEUE : remove the front element if the queue is not empty\n  - PRINT : print the current queue from front to rear\n\nRules:\n- If ENQUEUE is called when the queue is full, do nothing.\n- If DEQUEUE is called when the queue is empty, do nothing.\n- For each PRINT command:\n  - print EMPTY if the queue has no elements\n  - otherwise print all elements from front to rear separated by one space\n\nYour implementation must use an array in circular fashion.",
