    "description": "Write a Java program to simulate a queue stored in an array of fixed size N using circular indexing.\n\nThe queue must follow First In First Out order. Use two indices:\n- f: index of the front element\n- l: index of the last element\n\nInput format:\n- The first line contains two integers N and Q, where N is the queue capacity and Q is the number of operations.\n- Each of the next Q lines is one operation:\n  - ENQ x : insert integer x at the rear of the queue\n  - DEQ : remove the front element\n\nRules:\n- If ENQ is called when the queue is full, ignore that operation.\n- If DEQ is called when the queue is empty, ignore that operation.\n- The queue must use the array in circular fashion.\n\nOutput:\n- If the queue is empty after all operations, print:\n  EMPTY\n- Otherwise print three lines:\n  1. the elements of the queue from front to rear separated by one space\n  2. f=<front_index>\n  3. l=<last_index>\n\nYour program must correctly handle wrap-around cases.",
