    "title": "Describe Member Cards Using Overridden Role Information",
    "description": "Complete the class hierarchy so that each card object can describe itself through one parent-class method call.\n\nRequirements:\n- MemberCard stores owner and id.\n- MemberCard has a method getCode() that returns owner + \"@\" + id.\n- MemberCard has a method describe() that returns getCode() + \":\" + getRoleInfo().\n- StudentCard extends MemberCard and stores studyYear.\n- StaffCard extends MemberCard and stores yearsWorked.\n- Both subclasses must override getRoleInfo().\n\nRole rules:\n- For StudentCard:\n  - if studyYear == 1, return \"STUDENT-FRESHMAN\"\n  - otherwise, return \"STUDENT-YEAR\" followed by the study year\n- For StaffCard:\n  - if yearsWorked >= 5, return \"STAFF-SENIOR\"\n  - otherwise, return \"STAFF-JUNIOR\"\n\nThe main method reads n objects. Each object is stored in a MemberCard reference:\n- \"STUDENT owner id studyYear\"\n- \"STAFF owner id yearsWorked\"\n\nPrint describe() for each object on a new line.\n\nThis task checks that the correct overridden method is chosen at runtime based on the actual object type.",
    "source_chunk_ids": ["6a828d694c06195e57c865fd", "6a828d694c06195e57c86600"],
    "skeleton_code": [
      {
        "filename": "Main.java",
        "content": "import java.util.*;\n\nclass MemberCard {\n    protected String owner;\n    protected int id;\n\n    public MemberCard(String owner, int id) {\n        this.owner = owner;\n        this.id = id;\n    }\n\n    public String getCode() {\n        return owner + \"@\" + id;\n    }\n\n    protected String getRoleInfo() {\n        return \"MEMBER\";\n    }\n\n    public String describe() {\n        return getCode() + \":\" + getRoleInfo();\n    }\n}\n\nclass StudentCard extends MemberCard {\n    private int studyYear;\n\n    public StudentCard(String owner, int id, int studyYear) {\n        super(owner, id);\n        this.studyYear = studyYear;\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    protected String getRoleInfo() {\n        return \"\";\n    }\n}\n\nclass StaffCard extends MemberCard {\n    private int yearsWorked;\n\n    public StaffCard(String owner, int id, int yearsWorked) {\n        super(owner, id);\n        this.yearsWorked = yearsWorked;\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    protected String getRoleInfo() {\n        return \"\";\n    }\n}\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n        MemberCard[] cards = new MemberCard[n];\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            String type = sc.next();\n            String owner = sc.next();\n            int id = sc.nextInt();\n            int value = sc.nextInt();\n\n            if (type.equals(\"STUDENT\")) {\n                cards[i] = new StudentCard(owner, id, value);\n            } else {\n                cards[i] = new StaffCard(owner, id, value);\n            }\n        }\n\n        for (MemberCard card : cards) {\n            System.out.println(card.describe());\n        }\n    }\n}\n",
