    "description": "Write a Java program to simulate open addressing in a hash table using quadratic probing.\n\nUse a table of size M and the hash function h(x) = x % M. When inserting a key x:\n- First try index h(x).\n- If that cell is occupied, try (h(x) + i*i) % M for i = 1, 2, 3, ...\n- Stop when the key is placed into an empty cell.\n- If no empty cell is found after trying M positions in total, that insertion fails.\n\nThe table is initially empty.\n\nInput:\n- The first line contains two integers M and n.\n- The second line contains n non-negative integer keys.\n\nOutput:\n- Print the final table as M space-separated values, using -1 for empty cells.\n- On the next line, print the number of failed insertions.\n\nThis task checks how collisions are resolved by probing other positions instead of staying only at the original hashed index.",
