    "title": "Trace a Quadratic Probing Insertion Path",
    "description": "Write a Java program that traces how open addressing resolves one collision using quadratic probing.\n\nA hash table has size M. A key x uses the hash function h(x) = x % M.\nTo look for a place to insert x, probe positions in this order:\n(h(x) + i*i) % M for i = 0, 1, 2, ..., M-1.\n\nYou are given which table positions are already occupied. Your program must:\n- print every probed index in order, separated by one space\n- stop as soon as an empty position is found, or after M probes\n- print the insertion index on the next line if an empty position is found\n- print -1 on the next line if no empty position is found in those M probes\n\nInput format:\n- First line: two integers M and t\n- Second line: t distinct integers, the occupied indices\n- Third line: one integer x\n\nOutput format:\n- First line: the sequence of probed indices\n- Second line: the found empty index, or -1 if insertion fails",
