    "description": "Complete the class hierarchy so that different entry types provide their own string representation through method overriding.\n\nRequirements:\n- Entry stores a name.\n- Entry has a method show() that returns name + \"=\" + toString().\n- PointEntry extends Entry and stores x and y.\n- RangeEntry extends Entry and stores start and end.\n- Both subclasses must override toString().\n\nFormatting rules:\n- PointEntry prints coordinates as (x,y).\n- RangeEntry prints a range as [small,big], where small is the smaller of start and end, and big is the larger one.\n\nThe main method reads n objects. Each object is stored in an Entry reference:\n- \"POINT name x y\"\n- \"RANGE name start end\"\n\nPrint show() for each object on a new line.\n\nThis task checks overriding and dynamic binding because show() is defined in the parent class, but the actual toString() used at runtime depends on the object's real type.",
