    "title": "Quadratic Probing Reachability and Guarantee Check",
    "description": "Write a Java program that analyzes a quadratic probing pattern in an open-addressed hash table.\n\nFor a table of size M and a starting hash position k, the probe positions are generated by:\nposition(i) = (k + i*i) % M, for i = 0, 1, 2, ...\n\nYour program must:\n- Print all distinct positions visited, in order, starting from i = 0.\n- Stop when the next computed position has already appeared before.\n- On the next line, print GUARANTEED if both conditions are true:\n  1. M is prime\n  2. the table is at least half empty\nOtherwise print NOT GUARANTEED.\n\nThe number of currently occupied cells is given as occupied. A table is considered at least half empty when the number of occupied cells is at most half of M.\n\nInput:\n- One line containing three integers: M k occupied\n\nOutput:\n- First line: the distinct probe positions separated by spaces\n- Second line: GUARANTEED or NOT GUARANTEED",
