    "description": "Write a Java program to simulate inserting integers into a hash table of size M using open addressing with linear probing.\n\nUse the hash function h(x) = x % M.\n- If position h(x) is empty, insert the key there.\n- Otherwise, resolve the collision by trying the next positions in this order:\n  (h(x) + 1) % M, (h(x) + 2) % M, ...\n- Continue until an empty slot is found or all M positions have been checked.\n- If the table is full and the key cannot be inserted, record -1 for that insertion.\n\nInput:\n- The first line contains two integers M and N.\n- The second line contains N integers to insert.\n\nOutput:\n- Print one line containing N integers: the index where each key is inserted, or -1 if it cannot be inserted.\n- Print one more line containing the final hash table from index 0 to M-1, using -1 for empty cells.\n\nConstraints for this task:\n- Treat the hash table as initially empty.\n- Do not use Java's built-in HashMap or HashSet.\n- Keys are non-negative integers.",
