    "description": "Write a Java program that simulates hash table insertion with open addressing.\n\nUse a table of size M. For each key x, compute its initial position as h(x) = x % M. If that position is already occupied, resolve the collision by linear probing, meaning the next positions to try are:\n(h(x) + 1) % M, (h(x) + 2) % M, ...\n\nInsert keys in the given order. If a key cannot be inserted because every table position has been checked, skip that key.\n\nInput:\n- The first integer is M, the table size.\n- The second integer is n, the number of keys.\n- The next n integers are the keys to insert.\n\nOutput:\nPrint the final hash table as M integers separated by one space.\nUse -1 for an empty position.\n\nNotes:\n- Treat -1 as an empty slot in the table.\n- Keys are non-negative integers.\n- A collision must be resolved only by the probing rule above.",
