    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "title": "Build a Hash Table and Report a Quadratic-Probing Search",
    "description": "Write a Java program that manages a hash table of size M using open addressing with quadratic probing.\n\nFor every key x, its base hash is h(x) = x % M.\nIf a collision happens, probe positions in this order:\n(h(x) + i * i) % M for i = 0, 1, 2, ..., M - 1.\n\nTask:\n1. Insert the given n keys into the table in the given order.\n2. If a key cannot be inserted after trying all M quadratic probes, ignore that key.\n3. After all insertions, search for one query key using the same quadratic probing rule.\n\nSearch reporting rules:\n- If the key is found, print: FOUND index probes\n  where index is the table position and probes is the number of checked positions.\n- If the key is not found, stop the search when:\n  - you reach an empty slot, or\n  - you have already checked M probe positions.\n  Then print: NOT_FOUND probes\n\nOutput format:\n- First line: the final hash table as M integers separated by one space, using -1 for empty cells.\n- Second line: the search result in one of the two formats above.\n\nInput:\n- First integer: M\n- Second integer: n\n- Next n integers: the keys to insert\n- Last integer: the query key\n\nNotes:\n- Keys are non-negative integers.\n- The value -1 is only used to represent an empty slot in the table.",
    "source_chunk_ids": ["6a81d7efd103f7044396559e"],
    "skeleton_code": [
      {
        "filename": "Main.java",
        "content": "import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static int insertKey(int[] table, int key) {\n        int m = table.length;\n        int h = key % m;\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {\n            int pos = (h + i * i) % m;\n            if (table[pos] == -1) {\n                table[pos] = key;\n                return pos;\n            }\n        }\n\n        return -1;\n    }\n\n    public static String searchReport(int[] table, int key) {\n        int m = table.length;\n        int h = key % m;\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {\n            int pos = (h + i * i) % m;\n            int probes = i + 1;\n\n            if (table[pos] == key) {\n                return \"FOUND \" + pos + \" \" + probes;\n            }\n\n            if (table[pos] == -1) {\n                return \"NOT_FOUND \" + probes;\n            }\n        }\n\n        return \"NOT_FOUND \" + m;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int M = sc.nextInt();\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n\n        int[] table = new int[M];\n        Arrays.fill(table, -1);\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            int key = sc.nextInt();\n            insertKey(table, key);\n        }\n\n        int query = sc.nextInt();\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < M; i++) {\n            if (i > 0) System.out.print(\" \");\n            System.out.print(table[i]);\n        }\n        System.out.println();\n\n        System.out.println(searchReport(table, query));\n    }\n}\n",
