    "title": "Print Training Progress Reports with Overridden Methods",
    "description": "Complete the classes so that different participant objects can generate their own progress report through method overriding.\n\nRequirements:\n- Participant stores a name and the number of completed lessons.\n- Participant.report() returns: name@completedLessons\n- StudentParticipant extends Participant, adds bonusLessons.\n  - Its total progress is completedLessons + bonusLessons.\n  - If total progress is at least 10, report() returns: name@DONE@totalProgress\n  - Otherwise, report() returns: name@IN_PROGRESS@remaining, where remaining = 10 - totalProgress\n- MentorParticipant extends Participant, adds assistedGroups.\n  - If completedLessons is at least 8, report() returns: Mentor@name@READY@assistedGroups\n  - Otherwise, report() returns: Mentor@name@TRAINING@needMore, where needMore = 8 - completedLessons\n\nThe main method reads an integer n. Each of the next n lines has one of these forms:\n- S name completedLessons bonusLessons\n- M name completedLessons assistedGroups\n- P name completedLessons\n\nCreate the correct object for each line, store it in a Participant array, and print each object's report() result on a new line.\n\nThis task checks inheritance, method overriding, and polymorphic method calls through a parent-class reference.",
