    "title": "Print Rectangle and Box Dimensions with Overridden toString()",
    "description": "Complete the classes so that a Rectangle object and a Box object produce different string representations through method overriding.\n\nRequirements:\n- Rectangle has two integer fields: length and width.\n- Rectangle.toString() returns the text: length@width\n- Box extends Rectangle and adds one integer field: height.\n- Box.toString() must reuse the inherited Rectangle string and append @height.\n- In the main method, all objects are stored in a Rectangle array, so the result must rely on polymorphic method calls.\n\nInput format:\n- The first line contains an integer n.\n- Each of the next n lines is one of the following:\n  - R length width\n  - B length width height\n\nOutput format:\n- Print the result of calling toString() for each stored object on a new line.\n\nExample:\n- Rectangle with length = 4 and width = 5 prints 4@5\n- Box with length = 2, width = 3, height = 6 prints 2@3@6",
    "source_chunk_ids": ["6a7f640b682895cb6c9aff68", "6a7f640b682895cb6c9aff6c"],
    "skeleton_code": [
