    "title": "Print Mixed Dimension Objects with Overridden toString",
    "description": "Complete the classes so that different subclasses provide their own string form through method overriding.\n\nRequirements:\n- Class Dimension stores two integers x and y.\n- Dimension.toString() returns the text x + \"@\" + y.\n- Class ReversedDimension extends Dimension and overrides toString() so it returns y + \"@\" + x.\n- Class BoxDimension extends Dimension, stores one more integer z, and overrides toString() so it returns x + \"@\" + y + \"@\" + z. You should reuse the parent result with super.toString().\n\nThe main method reads an integer n, then reads n object descriptions:\n- NORMAL x y\n- REVERSED x y\n- BOX x y z\n\nStore all created objects in an array of Dimension and print each object on a new line. The output must rely on polymorphism, so calling toString() on the parent reference prints the correct subclass form.",
    "source_chunk_ids": ["6a7f640b682895cb6c9aff68", "6a7f640b682895cb6c9aff6c"],
    "skeleton_code": [
      {
        "filename": "Main.java",
        "content": "import java.util.*;\n\nclass Dimension {\n    protected int x;\n    protected int y;\n\n    public Dimension(int x, int y) {\n        this.x = x;\n        this.y = y;\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public String toString() {\n        return \"\";\n    }\n}\n\nclass ReversedDimension extends Dimension {\n    public ReversedDimension(int x, int y) {\n        super(x, y);\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public String toString() {\n        return \"\";\n    }\n}\n\nclass BoxDimension extends Dimension {\n    private int z;\n\n    public BoxDimension(int x, int y, int z) {\n        super(x, y);\n        this.z = z;\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public String toString() {\n        return \"\";\n    }\n}\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n        Dimension[] items = new Dimension[n];\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            String type = sc.next();\n            if (type.equals(\"NORMAL\")) {\n                int x = sc.nextInt();\n                int y = sc.nextInt();\n                items[i] = new Dimension(x, y);\n            } else if (type.equals(\"REVERSED\")) {\n                int x = sc.nextInt();\n                int y = sc.nextInt();\n                items[i] = new ReversedDimension(x, y);\n            } else if (type.equals(\"BOX\")) {\n                int x = sc.nextInt();\n                int y = sc.nextInt();\n                int z = sc.nextInt();\n                items[i] = new BoxDimension(x, y, z);\n            }\n        }\n\n        for (Dimension item : items) {\n            System.out.println(item.toString());\n        }\n    }\n}\n",
