    "description": "Complete the program so that it models two related classes.\n\n- Class Sheet stores two integer dimensions: width and height.\n- Its toString() method must return the text in the form width@height.\n- Class StackedSheet extends Sheet and adds one more integer field: layers.\n- StackedSheet must override toString() so that it returns width@height@layers. Use the parent result as part of the subclass result.\n\nThe main method reads several objects and stores them in an array of Sheet references.\n- If type = 1, create a Sheet using width and height.\n- If type = 2, create a StackedSheet using width, height, and layers.\n\nFinally, print the result of calling toString() for each object on a new line.\n\nInput format:\n- The first integer is n, the number of objects.\n- Each of the next n lines starts with type.\n- For type 1: type width height\n- For type 2: type width height layers",
