ns":[],"text":"[
  {
    "type": "PE",
    "topic_tags": ["polymorphism", "method overriding", "classes", "methods", "inheritance", "objects"],
    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "title": "Expand Mixed Packages with Overridden Methods",
    "description": "Complete the program so that it models two related classes using inheritance and overriding.\n\n- Class FlatPackage stores two integer dimensions: length and width.\n- Method expand(int value) increases both length and width by value.\n- Its toString() method returns the text in the form length@width.\n\n- Class BoxPackage extends FlatPackage and adds one more integer field: height.\n- BoxPackage must override expand(int value) so that all three dimensions increase by value. Reuse the parent behavior for length and width.\n- BoxPackage must also override toString() so that it returns length@width@height. Reuse the parent result as part of the subclass result.\n\nThe main method reads several objects and stores them in an array of FlatPackage references. Then it reads one expansion value and calls expand(value) for every object through the parent reference.\n\nFinally, print the result of calling toString() for each object on a new line.\n\nInput format:\n- The first integer is n, the number of objects.\n- Each of the next n lines starts with type.\n- If type = 1: type length width\n- If type = 2: type length width height\n- The last integer is the expansion value.",
