    "description": "Complete the class hierarchy so that a child class provides its own implementation of a method inherited from the parent class.\n\nRequirements:\n- Class Board stores two integers: rows and columns.\n- The constructor receives rows and columns.\n- Method expand(int addRows, int addColumns) adds the given values to rows and columns.\n- Method toString() in Board returns the text: rows@columns\n- Class LayeredBoard extends Board and adds one integer field named layers.\n- Its constructor receives rows, columns, and layers.\n- Method addLayers(int extra) adds extra to layers.\n- LayeredBoard must override toString() so that it returns: rows@columns@layers\n  You should reuse the parent result by calling super.toString().\n- In main, all objects are stored in a Board[] array, and toString() must be called through the parent type.\n\nInput format:\n- The first integer n is the number of objects.\n- Each of the next n lines is one of the following:\n  - 1 rows columns addRows addColumns\n  - 2 rows columns layers addRows addColumns extraLayers\n\nFor each object:\n- Create the correct object type.\n- Apply the update methods.\n- Store it in the array.\n\nOutput format:\n- Print the result of toString() for each object on a new line in the same order as input.",
