    "title": "Search a Hash Table Using Quadratic Probing",
    "description": "Write a Java program to search for a key in an open-addressed hash table.\n\nThe table has size M and stores integers. An empty slot is represented by -1. You are also given the already-computed base hash position h for the key to be searched.\n\nSearch the table using quadratic probing with the probe sequence:\nposition(i) = (h + i * i) mod M, for i = 0, 1, 2, ...\n\nRules:\n- If the key is found, print the index where it is found.\n- If an empty slot (-1) is reached before finding the key, print -1.\n- If all M probe attempts are used without finding the key, print -1.\n\nInput format:\n- First line: M\n- Second line: M integers describing the table\n- Third line: h target\n\nOutput format:\n- One integer: the found index, or -1 if the key is not found.\n\nExample behavior:\nIf M = 7, h = 3, the checked positions are 3, 4, 0, 5, 5, 0, 4 ... modulo 7 based on i^2.",
