    "title": "Build and Search an Open-Addressed Hash Table",
    "description": "Write a Java program that builds a hash table of size M using open addressing.\n\nUse these rules:\n- The hash function is h(x) = x % M.\n- If a collision happens at h(x), resolve it by probing the next positions using:\n  hi(x) = (h(x) + i) % M for i = 1, 2, ...\n- Store integers in an array of size M.\n- An empty slot is represented by -1.\n\nInput format:\n- The first line contains M and N.\n- The second line contains N distinct integers to insert into the hash table in the given order.\n- The third line contains Q.\n- The fourth line contains Q integers to search.\n\nRequired behavior:\n1. Insert all N keys using the probing rule above.\n2. Then search each query key using the same probing sequence.\n3. For each query, print the table index where the key is found, or -1 if it is not in the table.\n\nNotes:\n- If a key cannot be inserted after checking all M positions, ignore that key.\n- During search, stop when either the key is found, an empty slot is reached, or M positions have been checked.\n- Print all search results on one line, separated by spaces.",
