    "description": "Write a Java program that simulates a bounded queue stored in an array using circular indexing.\n\nThe queue has fixed capacity N and does not grow. Use First In First Out order.\n\nSupported commands:\n- ENQ x : insert integer x at the rear of the queue. If the queue is full, ignore this command.\n- DEQ : remove the front element. If the queue is empty, ignore this command.\n- REPORT : print the current queue state.\n\nQueue rules:\n- The array is used in circular fashion, so front and rear indices may wrap around.\n- Track the index of the front element and the index of the rear element in the underlying array.\n- When the queue is empty, both indices are considered -1.\n\nInput format:\n- The first line contains two integers N and M, where N is the queue capacity and M is the number of commands.\n- Each of the next M lines contains one command in one of the formats above.\n\nOutput format:\n- For every REPORT command, print exactly one line.\n- If the queue is empty, print:\n  - -1 -1 0 EMPTY\n- Otherwise print:\n  - frontIndex rearIndex size followed by the queue elements from front to rear, all separated by one space.\n\nNotes:\n- The queue is a fixed-size bounded circular queue.\n- Ignored commands produce no output by themselves.\n\nExample output line for a non-empty queue:\n0 2 3 5 8 9",
