    "description": "Write a Java program to simulate a bounded queue of service tickets using an array in circular fashion.\n\nThe queue has fixed capacity N and follows First In First Out (FIFO) order. You must manage the queue with array-based circular indexing.\n\nCommands:\n- ENQUEUE x : add ticket x to the rear of the queue. If the queue is full, ignore this command.\n- DEQUEUE : remove the ticket at the front of the queue. If the queue is empty, ignore this command.\n- FRONT : print the current front ticket. If the queue is empty, print EMPTY.\n- REPORT : print all current tickets from front to rear, separated by one space. If the queue is empty, print EMPTY.\n\nInput format:\n- The first line contains two integers N and M.\n- N is the fixed capacity of the queue.\n- M is the number of commands.\n- Each of the next M lines contains one command in the formats above.\n\nOutput format:\n- For each FRONT command, print one line.\n- For each REPORT command, print one line.\n- ENQUEUE and DEQUEUE produce no output.\n\nRules:\n- Implement the queue as a bounded circular array.\n- Do not use Java built-in queue classes.\n- If an ENQUEUE command happens while the queue is full, it must be ignored.\n- If a DEQUEUE command happens while the queue is empty, it must be ignored.",
