    "description": "Complete the program so that one parent class represents a text action and each subclass provides its own version of the same method.\n\nRequirements:\n- Class TextAction stores a text string.\n- Method process() is declared in TextAction and overridden in each subclass.\n- Method getReport() is inherited by all subclasses and must return the result of process() followed by a space and the original text length in parentheses.\n- Class ReverseAction overrides process() to return the text in reverse order.\n- Class UpperAction overrides process() to return the text in uppercase.\n\nThe main method reads two lines:\n- the first line is used to create a ReverseAction object\n- the second line is used to create an UpperAction object\n\nStore both objects in TextAction references and print getReport() for each object on separate lines.\n\nExample report format:\nreversedText (5)",
