    "title": "Calculate Different Booking Costs Using Overriding",
    "description": "Complete the program so that different booking types calculate their total cost through method overriding.\n\nRequirements:\n- Class Booking stores two integer fields: distance and passengers.\n- Method calculateCost() is defined in Booking and overridden in each subclass.\n- Method getReport() is inherited by all subclasses.\n- A booking is valid only when distance > 0 and passengers > 0. If a booking is invalid, getReport() must return \"INVALID\".\n- Otherwise, getReport() must return the calculated cost as an integer.\n\nSubclass rules:\n- BusBooking overrides calculateCost() with this rule:\n  - cost = distance * 5000 * passengers\n  - if passengers >= 3, apply a 10% discount to the total cost\n- TaxiBooking overrides calculateCost() with this rule:\n  - cost = 15000 + distance * 12000\n  - if passengers > 2, add 5000 for each passenger beyond 2\n\nThe main method reads four integers in this order:\n- busDistance busPassengers taxiDistance taxiPassengers\n\nCreate one BusBooking object and one TaxiBooking object, store them in Booking references, and print getReport() for each object on separate lines.",
