    "description": "Complete the program so that different subclasses decide whether a number in the same range should be counted.\n\nRequirements:\n- Class NumberCounter stores two integer fields: start and end.\n- Method isMatch(int n) is declared in NumberCounter and overridden in each subclass.\n- Method countMatches() is inherited by all subclasses. It counts how many integers from start to end (inclusive) satisfy isMatch(int n).\n- If start > end, countMatches() must return 0.\n- Class EvenCounter overrides isMatch(int n) to return true when n is even.\n- Class PrimeCounter overrides isMatch(int n) to return true when n is a prime number.\n- A prime number is greater than 1 and has exactly two positive divisors: 1 and itself.\n\nThe main method reads two integers: start and end.\nCreate one EvenCounter object and one PrimeCounter object, store them in NumberCounter references, and print countMatches() for each object on separate lines.",
