    "title": "Simulate Open Addressing with Linear Probing",
    "description": "Write a Java program to simulate insertion into a hash table using open addressing.\n\nUse a table of size M, initially empty. For each non-negative key x, compute its home position by h(x) = x % M.\nIf that position is already occupied, resolve the collision by linear probing:\n(h(x) + i) % M for i = 1, 2, 3, ... until an empty slot is found.\nIf every slot has been checked and no empty slot exists, that key cannot be inserted.\n\nInput:\n- The first line contains two integers M and N.\n- The second line contains N non-negative integer keys.\n\nOutput:\n- Print N integers: the index where each key is finally inserted.\n- Print -1 for a key that cannot be inserted because the table is full.\n- On the next line, print the final hash table contents from index 0 to M-1.\n- Use -1 for an empty slot.\n\nExample meaning:\nIf a key hashes to an occupied position, keep trying the next positions circularly until you find an empty one.",
