    "description": "Write a Java program that manages a hash table using open addressing.\n\nUse these rules:\n- Table size is M.\n- The hash function is h(x) = x mod M.\n- When a collision happens, probe the next positions using\n  hi(x) = (h(x) + i) mod M for i = 1, 2, 3, ...\n- This means the probing sequence is linear: start at h(x), then try h(x)+1, h(x)+2, ... modulo M.\n\nInput format:\n- The first line contains M and N.\n- The second line contains N integers to insert into an initially empty table.\n- The third line contains Q.\n- The fourth line contains Q integers to search.\n\nInsertion rules:\n- Insert keys in the given order.\n- If a key cannot be inserted because every slot has been tried, ignore that key.\n- Do not insert a duplicate key if it is already in the table.\n\nSearch rules:\n- For each query key, search using the same probing sequence.\n- If the key is found, print its index.\n- If the key is not found, print -1.\n\nOutput format:\n- First line: the final table contents from index 0 to M-1, using -1 for empty slots.\n- Second line: the search results for the Q query keys, separated by spaces.\n\nExample:\nIf M = 7 and keys 10, 17, 24 are inserted, they all hash to 3, so they are placed by probing indices 3, 4, and 5.",
