    "description": "Write a Java program that simulates collision resolution in a hash table using open addressing.\n\nThe table has size M and starts empty. For each arriving item, you are given its already-computed home position k. If position k is occupied, try the next positions using linear probing:\n(h(x) + i) mod M with i = 0, 1, 2, ..., M - 1.\n\nInsert the item into the first free slot found. If all M positions are occupied, output -1 for that item.\n\nInput:\n- The first line contains two integers M and n.\n- The second line contains n integers, where each integer is the home position k of one item.\n\nOutput:\n- Print n integers separated by spaces.\n- The ith output is the table index where the ith item is placed, or -1 if it cannot be placed.\n\nConstraints:\n- 1 <= M\n- 0 <= n\n- Each given home position satisfies 0 <= k < M",
