    "description": "Write a Java program that stores integer keys in a hash table using open addressing with quadratic probing, then answers search queries.\n\nHash rule:\n- Table size is M.\n- For a key x, its home index is h(x) = ((x % M) + M) % M.\n- If a collision occurs, probe using quadratic probing:\n  (h(x) + i * i) % M for i = 0, 1, 2, ..., M - 1.\n\nInsertion rules:\n- Insert each key into the first free slot found in its quadratic probing sequence.\n- If the key is already present in the table, do not insert it again.\n- If no free slot is found after M probes, ignore that insertion.\n\nSearch rules:\n- To search for a key, follow the same quadratic probing sequence.\n- If the key is found, print its table index.\n- If an empty slot is reached before finding the key, print -1.\n- If M probes are exhausted without finding the key, print -1.\n\nInput:\n- The first line contains two integers M and n.\n- The second line contains n integers: the keys to insert.\n- The third line contains an integer q.\n- The fourth line contains q integers: the keys to search.\n\nOutput:\n- Print q integers separated by spaces.\n- Each output value is the index where the queried key is found, or -1 if it is not in the table.",
