    "description": "Write a Java program to simulate one open-addressing insertion attempt.\n\nA hash table has size M. A new key has already been hashed to address h. If position h is empty, the key is placed there. Otherwise, use the given probe offsets p(1), p(2), ..., p(k) and try positions:\n(h + p(i)) mod M\nin that order until an empty position is found.\n\nThe table is represented by M integers:\n- -1 means the slot is empty\n- any other value means the slot is occupied\n\nInput:\n- integer M\n- M integers for the table\n- integer h (the original hashed address)\n- integer k\n- k integers representing the probe offsets\n\nOutput:\n- the index where the key will be placed\n- print -1 if no empty slot is found in the original position or in any probed position",
